    <exercise>
  <title>Exercise 4.4 (f)</title>
  <statement>
    <p>
      Prove by induction that for all natural numbers <m>n</m>,
      <md>1\cdot 1! + 2\cdot 2! + 3\cdot 3! + \dots + n\cdot n! = (n+1)! -1.</md>
    </p>
  </statement>
</exercise>
</page>
<page>

<exercise>
  <statement>
    <p>
      The Lucas Numbers are a sequence of natural numbers <m>L_1, L_2, L_3, \dots, L_n, \dots</m> which are 
      defined recursively as follows
        <ul>
          <li>
            <p>
              <m>L_1 =1</m> and <m>L_2 = 3</m>
            </p>
          </li>
           <li>
            <p>
              For each naturnal number <m>n</m>, <m>L_{n+2} = L _{n+1} + L_n</m>.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
    </p>
    <p>
    Find the first 10 Lucas numbers and the first 10 Fibonacci numbers and then prove that <m>L_n = 2f_{n+1}-f_n</m>
    for each natural number <m>n</m>.
    </p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>






</page>


</worksheet>